# An append-only log has no merge conflicts worth a human.
#
# `union` is built into git, so nothing needs configuring on any machine. It
# takes both sides and does not sort, which is why the tool that appends also
# re-sorts. Identical lines collapse to one, which is right for findings: the
# same gotcha seen twice is one gotcha. NOTHING EDITS A LINE IN THIS FILE.
# Union on a file where somebody edits an existing line is data loss with no
# conflict to warn about. After station-node's .gitattributes.
machines/kiosk-1/GOTCHAS.log    merge=union
